# Real-Time Voice Runtime

## Architecture boundary
Asterisk + SIP Edge + Pipecat are the realtime media path.
Django is the business/control plane.

Never move slow business workflows into the audio path.

## Call admission
Before production media is admitted, resolve:
- tenant/customer/agent;
- agent publish/active state;
- phone-number routing;
- plan/usage eligibility;
- compliance/recording policy;
- provider/runtime configuration.

The admission decision must be deterministic and observable.

## Call identity
Every live call carries:
- vokit_call_id;
- provider_call_id;
- tenant_id;
- customer_id;
- agent_id;
- correlation_id.

No runtime component may infer tenant identity from a caller-controlled header.

## Runtime resilience
- Bound external provider timeouts.
- Use safe fallback behavior for integration failures.
- Keep audio-path operations short and non-blocking.
- Use bounded concurrency and backpressure.
- Emit lifecycle events for started/answered/completed/failed and important tool actions.
- Reconcile provider terminal state with local call state.

## Billing/usage
Usage must be attributable to one call and one customer tenant scope.
The realtime worker must not directly invent money/ledger semantics.

## Deployments
Releasing the Django API must not silently invalidate Asterisk/SIP Edge/Pipecat contracts.
Media-path rollouts require compatibility verification and rollback strategy.
